## 🏗️ Architecture

The application follows Django's standard architecture:

```text
Client
  │
  ▼
Django URLs
  │
  ▼
Views
  │
  ├── Authentication
  ├── Authorization
  └── Business Logic
  │
  ▼
Models
  │
  ▼
Database
  │
  ▼
Template
  │
  ▼
HTML Response
```

---

## 📋 Job Management

Each job listing contains information required to represent an employment opportunity.

The main workflow is:

```text
Create
  │
  ▼
Publish
  │
  ▼
View
  │
  ├── Edit
  │
  └── Delete
```

Only the owner of a listing can modify or remove it.

---

## 👤 Authentication

The application provides user authentication using Django's authentication system.

Available functionality:

- Account registration
- Login
- Logout
- Authenticated sessions
- Protected routes
- User-specific job management

---

## 📊 My Jobs

Authenticated users have access to a dedicated area containing their own job listings.

```text
User
 │
 ▼
My Jobs
 │
 ├── Job 01
 │    ├── View
 │    ├── Edit
 │    └── Delete
 │
 ├── Job 02
 │    ├── View
 │    ├── Edit
 │    └── Delete
 │
 └── Job N
```

---

## 🎨 Frontend

The interface uses Django Templates with Bootstrap 5.

The application includes:

- Responsive navigation
- Dynamic navbar
- Reusable `base.html`
- Form interfaces
- Feedback messages
- Job listing pages
- User-specific pages

